 "evidence": [
  "List text: 'Red tile roof with gable at east end tile-hung above brick dentil band, with decorative barge boards ... 2 projecting wrought-iron sign brackets, one with decorative terminal ... a massive chimney at the west end, with painting on plaster at the 1st floor, and a carved fireplace on the ground floor in a room with panelled walls, all of C16.'",
  "Looked at, not copied (Commons: geograph 670559, 2998950, 670633, 956256): the tile-hung gable facing the street with pale bargeboards; the iron bracket over the pavement carrying a sign of St George and the dragon.",
  "List text: 'Large U-shaped late medieval timber-framed structure ... The rear extensions have exposed timber framing and more recent single-storeyed outshots with painted brick infill'."
